# dev/ is TRACKED. Design notes, prototype scripts, reference PDFs and small
# benchmark results belong in git so they travel between machines -- see the
# "do not add an ignore rule for something the maintainer produced or fetched
# by hand" rule in CLAUDE.md. Papers are tracked at whatever size they are.
#
# The exception is large REGENERABLE data: cohort matrices, cached downloads,
# serialized fixtures. Those are rebuilt from source, not authored, so losing
# them costs compute rather than work. They are listed below so a stray `git
# add dev/` cannot pull a hundred megabytes into history by accident.
#
# This file is allow-by-default on purpose. A new note or PDF dropped here is
# tracked with no further action; only the formats named below are excluded.

*.qs2
*.qs
*.rda
*.RData
*.fst
*.feather
*.parquet
*.h5
*.bigmemory
*.bin
